jobs.description:
Langan provides expert land development engineering and environmental consulting services for major developers, renewable energy producers, energy companies, corporations, healthcare systems, colleges/universities, and large infrastructure programs throughout the U.S. and around the world. Our employees collaborate seamlessly among 50+ offices and gain valuable hands-on experience that fosters career growth. Langan culture is entrepreneurial from advancing innovative technical solutions, to participating in robust training and knowledge sharing, to making progressive change within the communities we live and work.

Consistently ranked among the top ten “Best Firms to Work For” and Engineering News-Record’s top 50 firms worldwide, Langan attracts and retains the best talent in the industry. Employees thrive at Langan, a firm that fosters an inclusive and supportive work environment for all; prioritizes wellbeing, health, and safety; encourages volunteerism and philanthropy; offers workplace flexibility, along with carbon-neutral office spaces; and empowers individuals to contribute their skills and knowledge to make impactful contributions.

Job Summary

Langan is seeking an Environmental Field Technician
to join its collaborative team in Miami, FL
. This individual will serve a key function in providing responsible for taking care of field equipment and company vehicles, assisting in environmental field work by collecting field data and samples, construction oversight, and compiling data and preparing reports. In this role, you will have the opportunity to environmental investigation/remediation projects of varying sizes in Florida.

Job Responsibilities

Assists with conducting various types of environmental monitoring (water, air, asbestos, lead) using basic field instruments;
Assists with collecting samples, performing field tests and collecting and recording data;
Operates and maintains various remedial systems; such as drills, pumps, electrical equipment;
Assembles and maintains field equipment and systems; inspects equipment, troubleshoots as necessary;
Monitors construction projects by taking various tests to evaluate whether the contractor or
subcontractor has complied with job specifications;
Prepares a variety of standard logs, and field forms (such as drilling logs, field investigation dailies,
and chain of custody logs);
Assists with basic drafting using AutoCAD; and
Performs other duties as requested.

Qualifications

High School diploma or equivalent. Associate’s degree in Engineering Technology, Construction Management, or related field preferred;
2+ years of prior related experience preferred;
Hazwoper Certification, maintenance of annual physical and respirator fit test, annual Hazwoper 8-hour recertification, as required;
Ability to inspect equipment and troubleshoot defects in equipment or materials;
Familiarity with AutoCAD preferred;
Excellent written and verbal communication skills;
Strong attention to detail with excellent analytical, multitasking, and judgment capabilities;
Ability to effectively work independently and in a team environment;
Ability to occasionally work during evenings and/or weekends;
Ability to travel to various job sites and spend most, if not all of the work day on-site, as-required; and
Possess reliable transportation for client meetings and job site visits and a valid driver’s license in good standing.

Langan provides a rich array of programs and benefits to help its employees advance their careers and enhance the quality of their lives. Our comprehensive compensation package includes: full-time employment company paid medical, dental, and vision coverage; life insurance, short- and long-term disability insurance, and paid pregnancy disability leave; 401(k)/Roth with company match; paid time off including parental and military leave; employee referral and professional license bonuses; and educational reimbursement.

Langan offers employee resource groups; flexible work schedules; extensive training; wellness programs; buddy and mentoring programs; and much more!

Langan is committed to providing equal employment opportunities to all qualified applicants and employees, including individuals with disabilities and protected veterans. We believe that an inclusive workplace is essential for the well-being and success of our employees.

Please review our Applicant Privacy Notice at Collection to understand how we collect, use, and retain your personal information: https://www.langan.com/langan-notice-at-collection

